  "problemStatement": {
    "formal": "\\text{Generic Sylow elimination: for transitive } G \\le S_5 \\text{ containing a transposition, } |G| \\notin \\{10,20,40\\}. \\text{ Factor the three verbatim lemmas } \\mathtt{gal\\_card\\_ne\\_}\\{10,20,40\\} \\text{ into one } \\mathtt{sylow\\_elim\\_card} \\text{ parameterized by the group order, and refactor the parent } S_5 \\text{ proof to use it.}",
    "plain": "Factor the three verbatim Sylow-argument lemmas gal_card_ne_10/20/40 (from the verified Abel-Ruffini S5 proof of x^5-4x+2) into a single generic sylow_elim_card lemma parameterized by the group order, then refactor the parent to use it. Proof-abstraction of existing verified base cases; difficulty rated Low.",
    "whyMatters": "The abstracted lemma is a reusable Galois-theory fact about transitive subgroups of S_p with a unique Sylow p-subgroup, potentially contributable to Mathlib alongside the classical result that a transitive subgroup of S_p containing a transposition is all of S_p."
  },
  "knownResults": {
