  "knowledge": {
    "progressSummary": "COMPLETE: generic Sylow-elim core (arbitrary prime + non-simplicity) merged (#35245); parent S5 proof now refactored to use it (Docker-verified). Both halves of the seeker task done.",
    "builtItems": [
      "zpowers_sylow_normal in AbelRuffiniOQ04OQ01OQ03.lean — arbitrary-prime Sylow-elimination core: order p·m + p∤m + no-small-divisor ⇒ ⟨c⟩ (order-p) normal",
      "conj_mem_zpowers_sylow — every g normalizes ⟨c⟩ (general prime consequence)",
      "zpowers_order5_normal now a one-line corollary of zpowers_sylow_normal (p=5 instance)",
      "zpowers_index_eq in AbelRuffiniOQ04OQ01OQ03.lean — [G:⟨c⟩]=m (quotient order m) by prime cancellation, no huniq/normality needed",
      "not_isSimpleGroup_of_sylow in AbelRuffiniOQ04OQ01OQ03.lean — arbitrary-prime non-simplicity from the normal Sylow core (1<m)",
      "not_isSimpleGroup_order5 + capstone example — p=5 corollary and 'any group of order 40 with an order-5 element is not simple'",
      "absurd_conj_of_transposition helper in AbelRuffiniOQ04OQ01.lean: shared S5 finish turning the involution disjunction (τcτ⁻¹=c ∨ =c⁻¹) into False via transposition_not_normalizing_5cycle (c and c⁻¹=c⁴ both forbidden)",
      "Parent refactor removed ~180 lines of triplicated Sylow machinery; parent 1498->1337 lines, Docker-verified 0-sorry."
    ],
    "insights": [
      "Generalizing the fixed prime 5 to a variable prime p is NOT a rename: the two number-theoretic steps change tactic. n_p ≡ 1 (mod p) ⇒ n_p = 1 needs Nat.mod_eq_of_lt hp.out.one_lt to evaluate 1 % p (omega cannot do variable-modulus mod); index cancellation [G:P]·p = p·m ⇒ [G:P] = m needs Nat.eq_of_mul_eq_mul_right (omega cannot cancel a variable multiplier).",
      "The whole Sylow API (Sylow.card_eq_multiplicity, card_sylow_modEq_one, Sylow.card_dvd_index, IsPGroup.exists_le_sylow) is already prime-generic, so the group-theory skeleton transports verbatim; only the two ℕ-arithmetic steps required new lemmas.",
      "The normal Sylow p-subgroup is not just an intermediate step: it is a proper nontrivial normal subgroup, so any group of order p·m (p∤m, no small Frobenius divisor, 1<m) with an order-p element is NOT simple. This is the structural reason the x⁵-4x+2 Galois groups (orders 10,20,40) cannot be the simple A₅.",
      "IsSimpleGroup.eq_bot_or_eq_top_of_normal turns non-simplicity into a clean two-case refutation: ⟨c⟩=⊥ contradicts orderOf c=p>1 (via Subgroup.zpowers_eq_bot + orderOf_one), ⟨c⟩=⊤ contradicts index=m>1 (via Subgroup.index_top).",
      "The index [G:⟨c⟩]=m follows by pure counting (index_mul_card + Nat.eq_of_mul_eq_mul_right cancelling the prime p) with NO divisor hypothesis and NO normality — it just records that G⧸⟨c⟩ has order m.",
      "Parent AbelRuffiniOQ04OQ01.lean refactored to USE the generic core: the three gal_card_ne_10/20/40 lemmas now delegate to AbelRuffiniSylowElim.involution_conj_eq_self_or_inv, making the abstraction load-bearing (completes the second half of the seeker task)."
    ],
    "mathlibGaps": [],
    "nextSteps": [
      "Formalize the conjugation-action homomorphism G/C_G(c) ↪ (ZMod p)ˣ (cyclic of order p-1): would let one read off exactly which orders p·m force ⟨c⟩ central vs acted-on, sharpening the involution ±1 lemma to arbitrary automorphism order.",
      "Build the composition-series/solvability follow-up: non-simple + the order-m quotient is a stepping stone toward proving such groups are solvable when m has no simple composition factor."
    ]
  },
